/**
 * The `shape-outside` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines a
 * shape—which may be non-rectangular—around which adjacent inline content should wrap. By default,
 * inline content wraps around its margin box; `shape-outside` provides a way to customize this
 * wrapping, making it possible to wrap text around complex objects rather than rectangular boxes.
 *
 * Initial: none. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - margin-box: The background is painted within (clipped to) the margin box.
